docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:10730:- **Changed by `0126`:** the column `aggregates_recorded` and the trigger `report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable`, plus the child table `report_snapshot_aggregate`. See "P6 round-6 repair migration 0126" (added 2026-11-08, T-DG6-ARCH-16).
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14443:Recorded by T-DG6-ARCH-16 (2026-11-08; F-DG6-460) from the shipped `packages/db/migrations/0126_p6_report_snapshot_aggregate.sql` (T-DG6-BE-Z9; F-DG6-400). The column, constraint, index, trigger and grant texts below are `information_schema` / `pg_get_constraintdef` / `pg_indexes.indexdef` / `pg_get_triggerdef` output. They come from a disposable PostgreSQL 16.15 database with all 118 migrations applied (`docs/delivery/handbacks/DG6/T-DG6-ARCH-16-evidence/01-catalog-0126.log`). The design is ADR-0045 §3 (amendment of 2026-11-08) and ADR-0051 §2 (amendment of 2026-11-08, part A). The migration adds one table and one column to `report_snapshot` (0080, "P5 tables, slice F"). Where this section and the `0080` section differ, this section wins. T-DG6-BE-Z10 to BE-Z12B shipped no migration. Their changes to what the API returns for references to restricted records are read-time rules, recorded in ADR-0051 (amendment of 2026-11-08) and checked by `apps/api/test/support/sensitive-reference-inventory.ts`. No stored column changed.
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14445:## report_snapshot_aggregate
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14456:- **Migration:** `0126_p6_report_snapshot_aggregate.sql`. **API module:** `reporting` (`reports/restricted.ts` reads it, and the snapshot writer inserts it).
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14476:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_key` (UNIQUE): `UNIQUE (snapshot_id, section_key, record_type, record_id)`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14477:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_snapshot_fkey` (FK): `FOREIGN KEY (transformation_id, snapshot_id) REFERENCES report_snapshot(transformation_id, id) ON UPDATE RESTRICT ON DELETE RESTRICT`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14479:**Indexes:** `report_snapshot_aggregate_pkey` (`id`) and `report_snapshot_aggregate_key`: `UNIQUE (snapshot_id, section_key, record_type, record_id)`. The key also serves the read by snapshot.
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14483:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_append_only`: BEFORE DELETE OR UPDATE FOR EACH ROW → `p2_append_only()`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14484:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_append_only_truncate`: BEFORE TRUNCATE FOR EACH STATEMENT → `p2_append_only()`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14485:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_guard`: BEFORE INSERT FOR EACH ROW → `report_snapshot_child_guard()` (raises `report_snapshot_aggregate_same_transformation` or `report_snapshot_aggregate_creation_only`)
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14486:- `report_snapshot_aggregate_row_guard`: BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE FOR EACH ROW → `p2_row_guard()`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14492:| aggregates_recorded | boolean | NOT NULL | `true` | **New** (ordinal 38). It is true when the snapshot's aggregate records are in `report_snapshot_aggregate`, which holds for every snapshot written since `0126` (the column default). It is false for the snapshots that existed when `0126` ran: the column was added with default `false` and then given default `true`. For those, the API labels the aggregate sections conservatively, from every record of the section's types marked sensitive in the snapshot's transformation (`legacyAggregates`, `reporting/reports/restricted.ts`). That may over-label and never under-labels. Immutable after insert (`report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable`). Not in the API. |
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14496:- `report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable`: BEFORE UPDATE FOR EACH ROW → `report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable()`
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14500:**Backfill:** none. The only existing-row change is `aggregates_recorded = false` on the snapshots stored before `0126`. Content and `content_sha256` are unchanged.
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14506:| `report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable()` | 0126 | `search_path = public, pg_temp`; not `SECURITY DEFINER`. On UPDATE it raises `check_violation` with constraint `report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable` when `aggregates_recorded` changes. So no update can turn a recorded snapshot into a legacy one, or the reverse. | via trigger |
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14514:| Database | The `section_key` and `record_type` patterns, the per-snapshot UNIQUE key, the composite FK (same transformation), `report_snapshot_child_guard()` (creation transaction only), append-only, and the immutable `aggregates_recorded`. |
docs/architecture/data-dictionary.md:14516:| API, read (`documentForReader`) | The flag of each aggregate section is decided from its references plus its aggregate records, per reader: true, false, or absent when none is sensitive. When `aggregates_recorded` is false, the records come from `legacyAggregates`. |
