docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0051-p6-authorization-boundary-read-scope-sensitive-records-deep-links.md:304:  - A stored snapshot keeps them in `report_snapshot_aggregate` (migration `0126`; ADR-0045 §3, amendment of 2026-11-08).
docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0051-p6-authorization-boundary-read-scope-sensitive-records-deep-links.md:305:- **Legacy snapshots.** A snapshot stored before `0126` has `report_snapshot.aggregates_recorded = false`. Its aggregate sections are judged conservatively against **every** record of the section's types marked sensitive in its transformation (`legacyAggregates`). This is a deliberate superset: it may over-label, and it never under-labels. The column is immutable after insert.
