docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0045-p5-generated-outputs-report-snapshots-owner-updates-presentation-evidence.md:339:## Amendment (2026-11-08, T-DG6-ARCH-16; T-DG6-BE-Z9; F-DG6-400, F-DG6-460): the records a section's aggregate includes, and the new snapshot child table `report_snapshot_aggregate` (`0126`)
docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0045-p5-generated-outputs-report-snapshots-owner-updates-presentation-evidence.md:352:- **The new table `report_snapshot_aggregate`.** It has one row per (snapshot, section, record), UNIQUE `report_snapshot_aggregate_key`. Like the other snapshot children:
docs/architecture/adr/ADR-0045-p5-generated-outputs-report-snapshots-owner-updates-presentation-evidence.md:359:- **The new column `report_snapshot.aggregates_recorded`** (boolean, NOT NULL). It is true for every snapshot written since `0126` (the default) and false for those stored before. It is immutable after insert (`report_snapshot_aggregates_recorded_immutable`). When it is false, the API judges the aggregate sections against every record of the section's types marked sensitive in the transformation (`legacyAggregates`). That conservative superset never under-labels.
docs/api/openapi.yaml:27173:          description: "The sections of the zod mirror (packages/shared/src/schemas/report.ts). A section carries the read-time member includesRestrictedRecords (boolean) when it references a marked-sensitive record (a row, an item or a source; T-DG6-BE-Z7B, F-DG6-340) or when its aggregate figures include one (T-DG6-BE-Z9, F-DG6-400): the executive pack's metrics_<subject> and the executive dashboard's area_value include the dashboard facts' benefits and business cases, the executive dashboard's items_portfolio rows include the benefits allocated to each initiative, and the gate pack's criteria count unverified evidence items. It is true when the reader is not admitted to at least one of those records (rows and items naming them are omitted; totals and metrics are unchanged and the same for every reader; label access.includesRestrictedRecords), false when the reader is admitted to all, and absent when none is sensitive (the document is then returned unchanged). A live report takes the aggregate records from its assembly; a stored snapshot from report_snapshot_aggregate (migration 0126), or, for a snapshot stored before 0126 (aggregates_recorded false), conservatively from every record of those types marked sensitive in its transformation. The aggregate records are never shown. The member is never stored: content and contentSha256 are unchanged (ADR-0051 §2 'Totals and rollups', amendment of 2026-11-08; ADR-0045 §3; D-195 Q3)."
### ADR-0051 rows mentioning ReportDocument
90:| every section of `ReportDocument`: live report, snapshot GET and the generate, issue, discard and reissue bodies (T-DG6-BE-Z7B, T-DG6-BE-Z9) | the section references a marked-sensitive record through a row, an item or a source, **or its aggregate figures include one** (the executive pack's `metrics_<subject>`, the executive dashboard's `area_value` and `items_portfolio`, the gate pack's `criteria`; corrected 2026-11-08, T-DG6-ARCH-16: see the amendment of that date) | ADR-0045 §3 (amendments of 2026-11-06 and 2026-11-08) |
256:- **New paragraph "Which responses carry `includesRestrictedRecords`":** the six response schemas plus every `ReportDocument` section, each with its owning ADR. It also records that `AdoptionDashboard` filters but has no member, and why.
267:- the read-time section member `includesRestrictedRecords` on every `ReportDocument` section (`packages/shared/src/schemas/report.ts` `sectionBase`). In OpenAPI it is documented in the `ReportDocument.sections` description, because the section items are open `type: object`.
283:**Why.** F-DG6-460 (Low; REQ-S10-002) found that this ADR, the OpenAPI descriptions and the data dictionary still described the narrower report-section rule from before T-DG6-BE-Z9. They also did not record what T-DG6-BE-Z10, BE-Z10B, BE-Z11, BE-Z12 and BE-Z12B shipped under D-218, D-219, D-222 and D-223. This amendment records the shipped rules. No code changes. The §2 table row for `ReportDocument` and the sentence after "Totals that are the same for every reader" are corrected in place, with a pointer to this amendment.
394:**Contract.** Only description texts changed in `docs/api/openapi.yaml`, with no schema change: `ReportDocument.sections`, the condition `value` of `AutomationRuleContent`, and the per-field descriptions of the fields in B to E. `pnpm openapi:lint` passes with 932 operations. No gate needs reopening.
